{{!-- =====================================================
     PROPOSAL KICKOFF
===================================================== --}}

<main class="sasha-practice-page">

  <div class="sasha-container">

    {{!-- =================================================
         INTRODUCTION
    ================================================== --}}

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-hero">

      <p class="sasha-practice-page-eyebrow">
        PROPOSAL MANAGEMENT
      </p>

      <h1>
        Proposal Kickoff
      </h1>

      <p class="sasha-practice-page-intro">
        Start the proposal with the team aligned on why you are pursuing
        the work, who is responsible for what, and when each contribution
        must be complete.
      </p>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         QUICK FACTS
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-quick-facts"
    >

      <h2 id="kickoff-quick-facts">
        At a Glance
      </h2>

      <div class="sasha-practice-fact-grid">

        <article class="sasha-practice-fact-card">

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-label">
            TIME
          </p>

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-value">
            30–45 minutes
          </p>

          <p>
            Keep the meeting focused. The objective is alignment and
            commitment, not a lengthy discussion of every proposal detail.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article class="sasha-practice-fact-card">

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-label">
            BEST FOR
          </p>

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-value">
            Usual and Full Effort
          </p>

          <p>
            A kickoff is most useful when several people will contribute
            to the proposal and deadlines or responsibilities need to be
            coordinated.
          </p>

        </article>


        <article class="sasha-practice-fact-card">

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-label">
            OUTPUT
          </p>

          <p class="sasha-practice-fact-value">
            A committed proposal team
          </p>

          <p>
            Everyone leaves knowing why the firm is pursuing the work,
            what they own, and exactly when their contribution is due.
          </p>

        </article>

      </div>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         WHO PARTICIPATES
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-participants"
    >

      <div class="sasha-practice-page-heading-row">

        <div>

          <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
            WHO PARTICIPATES
          </p>

          <h2 id="kickoff-participants">
            Bring the people who will actually do the work.
          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <p>
          Invite the people whose decisions, writing, technical input,
          reviews, or production work will affect the proposal.
          You do not need every possible contributor in the room.
          Include the people who need to understand the pursuit and
          commit to the proposal plan.
        </p>


        <div class="sasha-practice-role-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Pursuit Leader
            </strong>

            <span>
              Explains why the opportunity is being pursued and confirms
              major decisions.
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Proposal Manager
            </strong>

            <span>
              Leads the proposal process, schedule, assignments, reviews,
              and production.
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Project Manager
            </strong>

            <span>
              Provides delivery insight and helps shape the technical
              response.
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Technical Leads
            </strong>

            <span>
              Confirm scope responsibilities, technical content, and
              contribution deadlines.
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Proposal Support
            </strong>

            <span>
              Writers, marketers, graphic designers, coordinators, or
              production staff who will help assemble the submission.
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-role">
            <strong>
              Other Key Contributors
            </strong>

            <span>
              Pricing, finance, reviewers, subconsultants, or specialists
              when their involvement needs to be coordinated early.
            </span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         STEPS
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-steps"
    >

      <div class="sasha-practice-page-heading-row">

        <div>

          <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
            THE PROCESS
          </p>

          <h2 id="kickoff-steps">
            Four things to accomplish
          </h2>

        </div>

      </div>


      <div class="sasha-practice-step-list">


        {{!-- STEP 1 --}}

        <article class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            01
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Review why this is a Go
            </h3>

            <p>
              Begin with a short review of why the firm chose to pursue
              the opportunity. The team should understand why the project
              is desirable and why the firm believes it can compete.
            </p>

            <p class="sasha-practice-step-note">
              This is also a final opportunity for someone to raise a
              serious concern before substantial proposal effort begins.
            </p>

          </div>

        </article>


        {{!-- STEP 2 --}}

        <article class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            02
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Confirm who is doing what
            </h3>

            <p>
              Identify the people contributing to the proposal and
              assign clear responsibilities.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Who owns each proposal section?
              </li>

              <li>
                Who supplies technical information?
              </li>

              <li>
                Who selects project and personnel evidence?
              </li>

              <li>
                Who reviews the work?
              </li>

              <li>
                Who manages graphics, pricing, production, and submission?
              </li>
            </ul>

          </div>

        </article>


        {{!-- STEP 3 --}}

        <article class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            03
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Build the schedule backwards
            </h3>

            <p>
              Start with the team's planned final production milestone,
              not simply the client's submission deadline.
            </p>

            <p>
              Work backward to establish contributor deadlines, review
              periods, proofreading, compliance checking, approvals,
              final production, and submission.
            </p>

          </div>

        </article>


        {{!-- STEP 4 --}}

        <article class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            04
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Get real commitments
            </h3>

            <p>
              Ask each contributor to confirm that they can meet the
              deadline assigned to them.
            </p>

            <div class="sasha-practice-callout">

              <strong>
                Avoid “I'll try.”
              </strong>

              <span>
                A proposal schedule only works when the people responsible
                for the work have actually committed to the dates.
              </span>

            </div>

          </div>

        </article>


      </div>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         VALUE
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-value"
    >

      <div class="sasha-practice-value-panel">

        <div class="sasha-practice-value-heading">

          <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
            WHY IT MATTERS
          </p>

          <h2 id="kickoff-value">
            The value is not the meeting.
          </h2>

        </div>


        <div class="sasha-practice-value-copy">

          <p>
            The value of a proposal kickoff is that the team begins with
            shared expectations instead of discovering them one deadline
            at a time.
          </p>

          <p>
            Clear responsibilities reduce confusion. Internal deadlines
            protect review and production time. Explicit commitments make
            it easier for contributors to plan proposal work alongside
            project responsibilities.
          </p>

          <p>
            Most importantly, the proposal becomes managed work instead
            of an emergency assembled immediately before submission.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         BEFORE THE MEETING
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-ready"
    >

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
          BEFORE YOU START
        </p>

        <h2 id="kickoff-ready">
          Have these five things ready.
        </h2>


        <div class="sasha-practice-check-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">
              ✓
            </span>

            <span>
              The RFP and current addenda
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">
              ✓
            </span>

            <span>
              The Go/No Go rationale
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">
              ✓
            </span>

            <span>
              The client submission deadline and time
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">
              ✓
            </span>

            <span>
              A preliminary list of contributors
            </span>
          </div>


          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">
              ✓
            </span>

            <span>
              A proposed internal production deadline
            </span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    {{!-- =================================================
         DECISION
    ================================================== --}}

    <section
      class="sasha-practice-page-section
             sasha-practice-page-decision"
      aria-labelledby="kickoff-decision"
    >

      <div class="sasha-practice-decision-panel">

        <div>

          <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
            ADD TO THIS PURSUIT?
          </p>

          <h2 id="kickoff-decision">
            Would you like to use a Proposal Kickoff?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Later, Sasha will use this choice to add the kickoff
            automatically to the proposal schedule.
          </p>

        </div>


        <fieldset class="sasha-practice-page-options">

          <legend class="visually-hidden">
            Use Proposal Kickoff
          </legend>


          <label>

            <input
              type="radio"
              name="useProposalKickoff"
              value="yes"
            >

            <span>
              Yes
            </span>

          </label>


          <label>

            <input
              type="radio"
              name="useProposalKickoff"
              value="no"
            >

            <span>
              No
            </span>

          </label>

        </fieldset>

      </div>

    </section>

  </div>

</main>